**COMMON MISTAKE:**

One common mistake that learners make when implementing responsive design is not using relative units for font sizes and margins. This can cause the web page to become distorted and difficult to read on smaller screens. Another common mistake is not using CSS media queries to apply different styles based on specific conditions. This can cause the web page to look the same on all devices, which can be frustrating for users.

